# S8-6 (PROBE): memory at EIGHT LIVE, on the traffic profile c2-packed-tp4-8 (the profile that is served: eight 123,136-token prompts, every seat live,
# then the short-prompt arm). The gate's memory plan: eight users, the profile's seats, each at the largest admitted prompt.
# READ: the DRAM ledger after every engine build ('dram-after-engine' lines: eight of them) and at the end of the arms; the floor and the largest free
# block per chip; the trace region's largest free block at 8 live; the DRAM hold's lines (a hold while a seat is free is a failed fit).
# KILL SIGNAL: free DRAM at 8 live below 3 GB per chip, or the floor below 1 GB. The second-window pool (262k windows) then falls below about five
# windows: take the block-only or the narrower-KV option before it. Pass: free at least 3 GB per chip, the floor at least 1 GB after eight engines, the
# trace region's largest free block at least 44 MB at 8 live. The ledger is saved: it is the measurement of the DRAM hold's three tunable bounds
# (QWEN_FAST_DRAM_PREFILL_TRANSIENT_MB, QWEN_FAST_DRAM_LARGEST_BUFFER_MB, QWEN_FAST_DRAM_ENGINE_BUILD_MB: unset today, so today's values).
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; the build and the two arms 35-60 min: 45 / 60 / 75 min. Stop rule: below the bars stops the window.
# SHIP WINDOW: pass bars as stated below, read on the shipping image: free at least 3 GB per chip at 8 live, the floor at least 1 GB, the trace region's
# largest free block at least 44 MB.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8 SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8 is the SHIPPING image: the base SB8 builds
# from this branch with the eight-seat profile baked in as its serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its
# seat count (ENV THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP). Every job serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still
# names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default. A commit that changes a file the image carries needs a new SB8 build and a
# new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-8
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8
C2_GATE_PLAN=memory
C2_GATE_JIT=record
